{#- EOS Segment Security (MSS-G, `router segment-security`): match-lists, field-sets, applications, the feature.

    `segment_security` (transforms/helpers/group_policy.py segment_security_device_view) is set only on a
    VTEP of a reference fabric that has a VRF with a segment to define; every block here is guarded by it, so
    a device without one renders exactly as before. Order (spec): global match-lists (one per segment, the
    segment's gateway prefix), field-sets and application traffic recognition (custom policies only), then
    `router segment-security`: the feature switch, the policies, and per VRF the segments with their
    definition and `from <source segment> policy <policy>` lines under the DESTINATION segment.
    Evidence: D is the EOS 4.36.2F manual (match-lists, segments, built-in policies, no shutdown); the custom
    policies, application l4, field-set l4-port, fallback policy come from Arista's AVD only, the rest is
    inferred; every such line says documented-not-lab-verified.
    Never rendered: `no segment policy policy-drop-all default` (removes deny by default for the whole box),
    redirect, log, `match interface`, uRPF. The anycast-gateway SVI ACL and PBR stay as they are. -#}
{%- if segment_security and (segment_security.vrfs or segment_security.skipped) %}
!
! Segment security (Arista MSS-G): segments by prefix, policies under the destination segment, deny by default
{%- if segment_security.staged %}
! {{ segment_security.staged }}
{%- endif %}
! documented-not-lab-verified: whether the lookup sees the inner IP of VXLAN-decapsulated traffic (spec 1.14, 5.1)
! documented-not-lab-verified: ordering against the SVI ACL and PBR (spec 1.15) and for bridged traffic inside a VLAN (spec 4.3)
! documented-not-lab-verified: no TCAM profile or reload is configured (spec 1.10, 1.12); enabling halves the LPM table
! documented-not-lab-verified: the manual calls the configuration non-atomic and disruptive (spec 1.8): push in a maintenance window
{%- for skipped in segment_security.skipped %}
! VRF {{ skipped.vrf }} is not rendered: {{ skipped.reason }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for text in segment_security.unsupported %}
! not expressible (left closed): {{ text }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if segment_security.vrfs %}
{%- for match_list in segment_security.match_lists %}
match-list input prefix-{{ match_list.family }} {{ match_list.name }}
   match prefix-{{ match_list.family }} {{ match_list.prefix }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for field_set in segment_security.field_sets %}
! documented-not-lab-verified: field-set l4-port is documented in AVD only
field-set l4-port {{ field_set.name }}
   {{ field_set.ports }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if segment_security.applications %}
! documented-not-lab-verified: application traffic recognition is documented in AVD only
application traffic recognition
{%- for application in segment_security.applications %}
   application l4 {{ application.name }}
{%- if application.field_set %}
      protocol {{ application.protocol }} {{ application.port_side }} port field-set {{ application.field_set }}
{%- else %}
      protocol {{ application.protocol }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
!
router segment-security
{%- if segment_security.enforce %}
   no shutdown
{%- else %}
   shutdown
{%- endif %}
{%- for policy in segment_security.policies %}
{%- if loop.first %}
   ! documented-not-lab-verified: custom policies are AVD's model (the 4.36.2F manual lists only policy-forward-all and policy-drop-all); the final drop of each is inferred
{%- endif %}
   ! {{ policy.name }}: {{ policy.text }}
   policy {{ policy.name }}
{%- for line in policy.lines %}
      {{ line.seq }} application {{ line.application }} action {{ line.action }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for vrf in segment_security.vrfs %}
   vrf {{ vrf.name }}
{%- for segment in vrf.segments %}
{%- if segment.remote %}
      ! documented-not-lab-verified: defined only because a policy of this device names it (a remote segment, spec 5.2)
{%- endif %}
      segment {{ segment.name }}
         definition
            match prefix-{{ segment.family }} {{ segment.match_list }}
{%- if segment.froms or segment.fallback %}
         policies
{%- for note in segment.notes %}
            ! {{ note }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for entry in segment.froms %}
            from {{ entry.source }} policy {{ entry.policy }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if segment.fallback %}
            fallback policy {{ segment.fallback }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
!
{%- endif -%}
